@startuml

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Modelling conventions
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' * Scope: the user facing public API of mw::com, reference for the FMEA
'   (dependability/safety_analysis/failure_modes.trlc).
' * The public API of a base class (*Base, Interface<Trait>) is flattened into
'   the user facing derived class.
' * Template parameters are in the quoted label; a parameter pack is one name
'   (ArgTypes).
' * Overloads get a name suffix (FindServiceBySpecifier / ...ByIdentifier).
' * One class per variant with a distinct API: ProxyMethod per partial
'   specialization; ProxyField* / SkeletonField* per field tag (tags with
'   identical API merged, e.g. ...WithNotifierOrGetter). A tag combination
'   offers the union of its variants.
' * Special members and operators (special members listed first, this order):
'   default ctor           -> ConstructDefault()
'   other ctor             -> Construct(...)
'   destructor             -> Destroy()
'   copy ctor / assign     -> CopyConstruct(other) / CopyAssign(other)
'   move ctor / assign     -> MoveConstruct(other) / MoveAssign(other)
'   converting move ctor   -> MoveConstructOther<Name>(...)
'   operator=(nullptr_t)   -> AssignNull()
'   explicit operator bool -> IsValid()
'   operator* / ->         -> Dereference() / MemberAccess()
'   operator()             -> Invoke()
'   operator== / !=        -> IsEqual() / IsNotEqual()
'   operator< / >          -> LessThan() / GreaterThan()
'   std::hash              -> Hash()
'   Free / friend operators are modelled on the type of the left hand side.
' * Visibility:
'   +  callable by the user
'   -  not callable (= delete, suppressed, implicitly deleted), or public in
'      C++ but not to be called by the user (ConstructDefault of SamplePtr /
'      SampleAllocateePtr). "-" does not mean C++ private.
' * Untyped parameter (e.g. IsEqual(other)): one operation for several C++
'   overloads; the note on the class lists them.
' * The commented line above each operation is its strict UML signature
'   (in / out / inout, multiplicity, {query} = const member function),
'   commented out because the tooling cannot parse it yet.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

